<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Bopfingen</h1><p class="st-meta">1241 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Bopfingen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the smallest imperial cities of the Empire, a Swabian market town at the foot of the Ipf, a celebrated Celtic hillfort.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bopfingen lies beneath the Ipf, a hill crowned by a major Celtic princely seat of the 6th and 5th centuries BCE. The medieval town grew under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> and appears among the imperial cities in the imperial tax list of 1241.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Bopfingen was a modest market town with a tiny territory, governed by a council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> and dependent on its larger neighbour <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-nordlingen">Nördlingen</a> and on the Swabian city leagues. Its economy rested on farming, crafts and the local market. It adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in the 16th century and suffered heavily in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years War.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Bopfingen lost its freedom in 1802, passing first to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-bavaria">Electorate of Bavaria</a> and in 1810 to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg">Kingdom of Württemberg</a>. It is now a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, and the Ipf is a protected archaeological site.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1241 CE – 1802 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.40%;width:11.16%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true